# promise: #424
# A double-click on the name of a pinned tab with no page opens the rename field, and what is
# typed next goes into it. The first press switches to the tab and starts its page; the page
# arrives after the second press has opened the field. Before the fix, the page took the
# keyboard as it arrived (on CEF its own window became key, on the engine its view became the
# window's first responder), so the typed name never reached the field and the tab kept its
# old name. No spare page here: a spare is ready at once, and the page has to arrive late.
budget rss=800 stalls50=12
env CRA_SPARE_PAGES=0
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=today
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=pinned
wait 1.5
cra://action/pinTab
wait 1
# Closing a pinned tab keeps its row and lets its page go (Arc), and Today's tab opens.
cra://action/closeTab
wait 2
expect-log closes its page
# The pinned tab is the first row (8,234, 312x40); its title starts past the 18 pt favicon.
cra://debug?snapshot=TabRowView&out=/dev/null
expect-log snapshot: TabRowView at 8,234 size 312x40
cra://debug?clickAt=150,254&clicks=2
expect-log sidebar double-click: rename
# Let the new page arrive while the field is open.
wait 3
cra://debug?zoomLevel=1
cra://debug?key=Q,12,0
cra://debug?key=x,7,0
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,0
wait 1
expect-log sidebar rename: new name, 2 characters
cra://debug?checkStore=1
